ARM_FILES = {'sq1c2a6i': {'agent.yaml': '# sq1c2a6i = sq1 with the clock shell (skills/work, scripts/run.py) instead of run_command; sq1: SequentialAgent [fixer, finisher] (scripts/make_skill_arms.py sq2): the fixer (pub024 procedure) never\n# submits and hands over in plain text; the finisher only submits (sq2 without the second attempt).\nname: swe_agent\nagent_class: SequentialAgent\nsub_agents:\n  - config_path: fixer.yaml\n  - config_path: finisher.yaml\n', 'configs/sampling.yaml': 'temperature: 0.2\ntop_p: 0.95\nmax_output_tokens: 8192\nthinking_config:\n  thinking_budget: 4096\n  include_thoughts: true\n', 'eval_config.yaml': 'evaluation:\n  timeout_seconds: 240\n  max_tool_calls: 80\n  max_time_minutes: 6\n  max_turns: 400\n', 'finisher.yaml': "name: finisher\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ninstruction: !include prompts/finisher.md\ninclude_contents: none  # fresh: its context starts at the fixer's hand-over line\ntools:\n  - run_command\n  - read_file\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch  # declared on all: the harness task message names it; an undeclared call drops the patch\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n", 'fixer.yaml': 'name: fixer\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ninstruction: !include prompts/fixer.md\ntools:  # no run_command: the shell is run_skill_script work scripts/run.py (clock line in every output)\n  - read_file  # named in the harness task message\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch  # declared on all: the harness task message names it; an undeclared call drops the patch\n  - get_code_neighbors\n  - search_similar_code\n  - get_code_subgraph\nskills:\n  - skills/work\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n', 'prompts/finisher.md': 'You submit this task: an engineer has just fixed the issue in /workspace, and the last message says\nwhat changed. The fix is final. You do not read, run or edit anything.\n\nYour only tool call: submit_patch. Then reply with one sentence and make no further tool calls.\n', 'prompts/fixer.md': 'You are an autonomous software engineer in /workspace. Your job: the smallest correct change to the SOURCE code so\nthat the hidden tests for the issue pass. Those tests were written from the issue text, so every exact name, message,\ntype and behaviour it mentions is the specification. A teammate submits your patch when you are done; you never call\nsubmit_patch.\n\n# YOUR TOOLS\n- Shell: run_skill_script with skill_name work, file_path scripts/run.py and positional_args, a list holding one\n  string: the whole shell command. Do not use the args parameter. Commands run in /workspace; this is your only way\n  to run them.\n- read_file reads part of a file, edit_file changes a file, write_file creates a scratch file.\n- Every shell result ends with a clock line, "[clock] N s of 360 used | ...": the time used, whether a source file is\n  edited, and what to do next. Read it every time and follow it. You have 6 minutes and most of that time goes into\n  your own thinking, so keep replies short.\n- If a tool says an argument is required, your call was malformed: send it again with every argument written out\n  plainly, never the same broken call twice.\n\n# LIMITS\n- The edit in /workspace when the session ends is what gets graded; an unedited tree scores zero. Edit a source file\n  before 180 s on the clock. If unsure, make your best-guess edit in the most likely place: a wrong edit can still be\n  corrected. With no source edit at 270 s the shell refuses commands until you edit.\n- When the clock says REPRO PASSES, run at most one related test file, then finish. A minute later the shell runs\n  only finishing commands (git status, git diff, git checkout -- TESTFILE, rm SCRATCHFILE); edit_file still works for\n  a last correction.\n- Never create, change or delete test files (test_*.py, *_test.py, anything under tests/, pytest.ini, conftest.py).\n- Scratch files only in /tmp or .git/agent/: any other new file under /workspace becomes part of the patch.\n- Never run a whole test suite: name one test file, and add -k when you can.\n- Never use search_similar_code, get_code_neighbors or get_code_subgraph: they return nothing useful.\n\n# TIME PLAN (by the clock line)\n- Up to about 120 s: locate and read. By 180 s: your edit is in the file.\n- Then: write the repro and run it; when the clock says REPRO PASSES, at most one related test file; then FINISH.\n- From 320 s: stop and FINISH whatever state you are in.\n\n# PROCEDURE\n1. From THE ISSUE at the end of these instructions, note for yourself the exact file, function, class or CLI name, the\n   exact error message and exception type, the expected return value or output, the inputs that trigger the bug and\n   every edge case it mentions. Each concrete string and name in it must appear exactly like that in your code.\n2. Locate. Use paths the issue names directly. Put independent searches for the issue\'s symbols, their callers and\n   relevant tests into one shell command: git grep -n -F "symbol" and git ls-files, about 20 output lines each. Then\n   read the implementation plus one caller or test, about 40 lines per region, at most three regions per command\n   (sed -n \'START,ENDp\' FILE). For a bug, find where the wrong behaviour is produced; for a feature, copy the closest\n   existing sibling, including __all__, option lists, dispatch tables and imports.\n3. Edit with edit_file, with a short, unique old_string copied exactly. If it fails twice, run one inline python script\n   through the shell (quoted heredoc) that asserts the old text occurs once, replaces it and writes the file. Fix the\n   cause, not the symptom; change only what the issue requires and keep signatures and defaults. Apply the change to\n   every parallel implementation (sync and async, each backend, re-exports in __init__.py or __all__). Use the issue\'s\n   exact exception class and message text. For FastAPI documentation tasks, edit docs_src/.\n4. Repro: write_file .git/agent/repro_a.py, a short script that imports the package normally, FAILS (assert or raise)\n   while the bug is there and prints FIXED on its own line only once it is fixed, otherwise BUG. Run it:\n   timeout 30 python3 .git/agent/repro_a.py\n5. If one related test file exists, run it once: timeout 120 python -m pytest tests/path/test_x.py -x -q -k keyword\n   Failures from missing fixtures or unrelated imports were there before you: ignore them.\n\n# FINISH\n1. One shell command: git status --short && git diff. Remove any scratch file in /workspace; restore any changed test\n   file with git checkout -- path.\n2. Reply in plain text with NO tool call: one line saying what you changed and where. That reply hands over to your\n   teammate.\n\n# DECISION RULES\n- Ambiguous issue: take the most literal reading and act on it. Never ask questions.\n- Several candidate places: choose where the wrong behaviour is produced, not where it is observed.\n- A fix failed: make a different, smaller change. Never repeat the same edit.\n- Never conclude that nothing needs to change: every task needs a non-empty source patch.\n\n# THE ISSUE (verbatim; the task message may later be replaced by a summary, this copy stays)\n{problem_description}\n', 'skills/work/SKILL.md': '---\nname: work\ndescription: The fixer\'s shell. run_skill_script with skill_name work, file_path scripts/run.py and positional_args,\n  a list holding one string, the whole shell command. Runs in /workspace; the output ends with a clock line.\n---\n\nscripts/run.py runs one shell command in /workspace (output cut at 5000 characters) and ends with\n"[clock] N s of 360 used | ..." saying whether a source file is edited and what to do next. With no source edit at\n270 s it refuses commands until edit_file has changed a source file. 60 s after the repro prints FIXED it runs only\nfinishing commands (git status, git diff, git checkout --, rm).\n', 'skills/work/scripts/run.py': '"""sq1c2f6\'s shell (skill "work", scripts/run.py): sq1c2\'s clock shell plus two finish events, so runs end sooner\nwithout touching the first 270 s. Every output ends with a clock line (time used, source edited or not).\n\n- Before 270 s: as sq1c2 (warning from 180 s with no source edit, refusal from 270 s until a source file is edited).\n- Event A: a command prints a line starting with FIXED (the repro passes) while a source file is edited -> the clock\n  says to finish; FIXED_GRACE s later the finish window opens.\n- Event B: from FINISH_AT s with a source file edited, the finish window opens.\n- In the finish window only finishing commands run (git status / git diff / git checkout -- / rm); edit_file still\n  works, so a last correction is possible.\n\n    run_skill_script skill_name=work file_path=scripts/run.py positional_args=["git grep -n foo"]\n"""\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nSESSION = 360  # max_time_minutes 6 (sq1c2a6)\nWARN_AT = 180  # as sq1c2: no source edit by now -> warn\nREFUSE_AT = 270  # as sq1c2: no source edit by now -> refuse commands until one exists\nFINISH_AT = None  # sq1c2a6: event B off\nFIXED_GRACE = 60  # event A: finish window opens this long after the repro first printed FIXED\nOUT_MAX = 5000  # as the harness\'s run_command output limit\nEDIT_CMD = re.compile(r"sed -i|git apply|\\bpatch\\b|open\\([^)]*[\'\\"][wa][\'\\"]|write_text\\(|>\\s*(?!/tmp|/dev/null|&)\\S")\nFINISH_CMD = re.compile(r"^\\s*(git (status|diff|checkout --)|rm )[^;|&`$\\n]*(&&\\s*git (status|diff)[^;|&`$\\n]*)*$")\nFIXED_RE = re.compile(r"^\\s*FIXED\\b", re.M)\nTEST_RE = re.compile(r"(^|/)(tests?|testing)/|(^|/)test_[^/]*\\.py$|_test\\.py$|(^|/)conftest\\.py$|(^|/)pytest\\.ini$")\n\n\ndef workspace():\n    """The repository root: the skill wrapper chdirs into a temp dir, so find the directory it started in."""\n    import inspect\n    for frame in inspect.stack():\n        cwd = frame.frame.f_locals.get("_orig_cwd")\n        if isinstance(cwd, str) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cwd, ".git")):\n            return cwd\n    for cand in ("/workspace", os.getcwd()):\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cand, ".git")):\n            return cand\n    return os.getcwd()\n\n\ndef run_group(cmd, ws, timeout):\n    """bash -c CMD in its own process group; the whole group is killed when the command ends or times out, as the\n    harness\'s run_command does (adk_eval_core subprocess_sandbox.py), so no runaway child outlives the call\n    (2026-11-02: an orphaned process froze a Kaggle run: tool calls slowed to 27 s, then no model calls at all)."""\n    p = subprocess.Popen(["bash", "-c", cmd], cwd=ws, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, start_new_session=True)\n    timed_out = False\n    try:\n        out, err = p.communicate(timeout=timeout)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        timed_out = True\n    try:\n        os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):\n        pass\n    if timed_out:\n        try:\n            out, err = p.communicate(timeout=5)\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            out, err = "", ""\n    return p.returncode, out or "", err or "", timed_out\n\n\ndef sh(cmd, ws, timeout=30):\n    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=ws, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n    return r.returncode, r.stdout\n\n\ndef state_path(ws):\n    return os.path.join(ws, ".git", "agent", "clock.json")\n\n\ndef load_state(ws):\n    try:\n        return json.load(open(state_path(ws)))\n    except Exception:\n        return {}\n\n\ndef save_state(ws, state):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(state_path(ws)), exist_ok=True)\n    json.dump(state, open(state_path(ws), "w"))\n\n\ndef started(ws, state):\n    """Session start: the harness tags _swegemma_baseline when the sandbox starts; else the first run.py call."""\n    code, out = sh(["git", "log", "-1", "--format=%ct", "_swegemma_baseline"], ws)\n    if code == 0 and out.strip().isdigit():\n        return int(out.strip())\n    if "t0" not in state:\n        state["t0"] = time.time()\n        save_state(ws, state)\n    return state["t0"]\n\n\ndef edited(ws):\n    """Changed or new source files (not tests, not scratch files)."""\n    _, out = sh(["git", "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all"], ws)\n    files = [line[3:].split(" -> ")[-1].strip(\'"\') for line in out.splitlines() if len(line) > 3]\n    return [f for f in files if not TEST_RE.search(f) and not os.path.basename(f).startswith("repro")]\n\n\ndef command():\n    """The command from positional args (or args {"cmd": "..."}, argv --cmd X)."""\n    argv = [a for a in sys.argv[1:] if a != "--"]\n    if argv[:1] == ["--cmd"]:\n        argv = argv[1:]\n    elif argv[:1] and argv[0].startswith("--"):\n        argv = argv[1:]\n    return " ".join(argv).strip()\n\n\ndef finish_opens(used, state):\n    """Seconds into the session at which the finish window opens (given a source edit)."""\n    opens = float(\'inf\') if FINISH_AT is None else FINISH_AT\n    if "fixed_at" in state:\n        opens = min(opens, state["fixed_at"] + FIXED_GRACE)\n    return opens\n\n\ndef main():\n    ws = workspace()\n    state = load_state(ws)\n    used = int(time.time() - started(ws, state))\n    cmd = command()\n    files = edited(ws)\n    if not cmd:\n        body = "NO COMMAND: pass it as positional_args, a list holding one string: the whole shell command."\n    elif not files and used >= REFUSE_AT and not EDIT_CMD.search(cmd):\n        body = (f"REFUSED: {used} s of {SESSION} used and no source file is edited yet. An unedited tree scores zero; "\n                "a best guess can still be corrected. Your next call must be edit_file on the most likely place "\n                "(where the wrong behaviour is produced). Commands run again once a source file is edited.")\n    elif files and used >= finish_opens(used, state) and not FINISH_CMD.match(cmd):\n        body = (f"REFUSED: FINISH NOW ({used} s of {SESSION} used, source edited: {\', \'.join(files[:4])}). Only "\n                "git status, git diff, git checkout -- TESTFILE and rm SCRATCHFILE run now. Check the diff once, "\n                "then reply in plain text with no tool call: one line on what you changed and where.")\n    else:\n        code, out, err, timed_out = run_group(cmd, ws, max(5, min(150, SESSION - used - 10)))\n        body = (out + (("\\n[stderr]\\n" + err) if err.strip() else "")).rstrip()\n        body += "\\n[timed out: the command and everything it started were stopped]" if timed_out else f"\\n[exit {code}]"\n        if len(body) > OUT_MAX:\n            body = body[:OUT_MAX] + f"\\n[output cut at {OUT_MAX} characters: narrow the command]"\n        files = edited(ws)\n        if files and "fixed_at" not in state and FIXED_RE.search(body):\n            state["fixed_at"] = used\n            save_state(ws, state)\n    if files and used >= finish_opens(used, state):\n        state_txt = "source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4]) + " | FINISH NOW: git status && git diff, then the one-line reply"\n    elif files and "fixed_at" in state:\n        state_txt = ("source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4]) + f" | REPRO PASSES: run at most one related test file, "\n                     f"then FINISH; from {finish_opens(used, state)} s only finishing commands run")\n    elif files:\n        state_txt = "source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4])\n    elif used >= WARN_AT:\n        state_txt = (f"NO SOURCE EDIT YET. Make your best edit now with edit_file; at {REFUSE_AT} s commands are "\n                     "refused until a source file is edited")\n    else:\n        state_txt = "no source edit yet"\n    print(body + f"\\n[clock] {used} s of {SESSION} used | {state_txt}")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n'}, 'sq1c2a6info': {'agent.yaml': '# sq1c2a6info = sq1 with the clock shell (skills/work, scripts/run.py) instead of run_command; sq1: SequentialAgent [fixer, finisher] (scripts/make_skill_arms.py sq2): the fixer (pub024 procedure) never\n# submits and hands over in plain text; the finisher only submits (sq2 without the second attempt).\nname: swe_agent\nagent_class: SequentialAgent\nsub_agents:\n  - config_path: fixer.yaml\n  - config_path: finisher.yaml\n', 'configs/sampling.yaml': 'temperature: 0.2\ntop_p: 0.95\nmax_output_tokens: 8192\nthinking_config:\n  thinking_budget: 4096\n  include_thoughts: true\n', 'eval_config.yaml': 'evaluation:\n  timeout_seconds: 240\n  max_tool_calls: 80\n  max_time_minutes: 6\n  max_turns: 400\n', 'finisher.yaml': "name: finisher\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ninstruction: !include prompts/finisher.md\ninclude_contents: none  # fresh: its context starts at the fixer's hand-over line\ntools:\n  - run_command\n  - read_file\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch  # declared on all: the harness task message names it; an undeclared call drops the patch\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n", 'fixer.yaml': 'name: fixer\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ninstruction: !include prompts/fixer.md\ntools:  # no run_command: the shell is run_skill_script work scripts/run.py (clock line in every output)\n  - read_file  # named in the harness task message\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch  # declared on all: the harness task message names it; an undeclared call drops the patch\n  - get_code_neighbors\n  - search_similar_code\n  - get_code_subgraph\nskills:\n  - skills/work\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n', 'prompts/finisher.md': 'You submit this task: an engineer has just fixed the issue in /workspace, and the last message says\nwhat changed. The fix is final. You do not read, run or edit anything.\n\nYour only tool call: submit_patch. Then reply with one sentence and make no further tool calls.\n', 'prompts/fixer.md': 'You are an autonomous software engineer in /workspace. Your job: the smallest correct change to the SOURCE code so\nthat the hidden tests for the issue pass. Those tests were written from the issue text, so every exact name, message,\ntype and behaviour it mentions is the specification. A teammate submits your patch when you are done; you never call\nsubmit_patch.\n\n# YOUR TOOLS\n- Shell: run_skill_script with skill_name work, file_path scripts/run.py and positional_args, a list holding one\n  string: the whole shell command. Do not use the args parameter. Commands run in /workspace; this is your only way\n  to run them.\n- read_file reads part of a file, edit_file changes a file, write_file creates a scratch file.\n- Every shell result ends with a clock line, "[clock] N s of 360 used | ...": the time used, whether a source file is\n  edited, and what to do next. Read it every time and follow it. You have 6 minutes and most of that time goes into\n  your own thinking, so keep replies short.\n- If a tool says an argument is required, your call was malformed: send it again with every argument written out\n  plainly, never the same broken call twice.\n\n# LIMITS\n- The edit in /workspace when the session ends is what gets graded; an unedited tree scores zero. Edit a source file\n  before 180 s on the clock. If unsure, make your best-guess edit in the most likely place: a wrong edit can still be\n  corrected. With no source edit at 270 s the shell refuses commands until you edit.\n- When the clock says REPRO PASSES, run at most one related test file, then finish. A minute later the shell runs\n  only finishing commands (git status, git diff, git checkout -- TESTFILE, rm SCRATCHFILE); edit_file still works for\n  a last correction.\n- Never create, change or delete test files (test_*.py, *_test.py, anything under tests/, pytest.ini, conftest.py).\n- Scratch files only in /tmp or .git/agent/: any other new file under /workspace becomes part of the patch.\n- Never run a whole test suite: name one test file, and add -k when you can.\n- Never use search_similar_code, get_code_neighbors or get_code_subgraph: they return nothing useful.\n\n# TIME PLAN (by the clock line)\n- Up to about 120 s: locate and read. By 180 s: your edit is in the file.\n- Then: write the repro and run it; when the clock says REPRO PASSES, at most one related test file; then FINISH.\n- From 320 s: stop and FINISH whatever state you are in.\n\n# PROCEDURE\n1. From THE ISSUE at the end of these instructions, note for yourself the exact file, function, class or CLI name, the\n   exact error message and exception type, the expected return value or output, the inputs that trigger the bug and\n   every edge case it mentions. Each concrete string and name in it must appear exactly like that in your code.\n2. Locate. Use paths the issue names directly. Put independent searches for the issue\'s symbols, their callers and\n   relevant tests into one shell command: git grep -n -F "symbol" and git ls-files, about 20 output lines each. Then\n   read the implementation plus one caller or test, about 40 lines per region, at most three regions per command\n   (sed -n \'START,ENDp\' FILE). For a bug, find where the wrong behaviour is produced; for a feature, copy the closest\n   existing sibling, including __all__, option lists, dispatch tables and imports.\n3. Edit with edit_file, with a short, unique old_string copied exactly. If it fails twice, run one inline python script\n   through the shell (quoted heredoc) that asserts the old text occurs once, replaces it and writes the file. Fix the\n   cause, not the symptom; change only what the issue requires and keep signatures and defaults. Apply the change to\n   every parallel implementation (sync and async, each backend, re-exports in __init__.py or __all__). Use the issue\'s\n   exact exception class and message text. For FastAPI documentation tasks, edit docs_src/.\n4. Repro: write_file .git/agent/repro_a.py, a short script that imports the package normally, FAILS (assert or raise)\n   while the bug is there and prints FIXED on its own line only once it is fixed, otherwise BUG. Run it:\n   timeout 30 python3 .git/agent/repro_a.py\n5. If one related test file exists, run it once: timeout 120 python -m pytest tests/path/test_x.py -x -q -k keyword\n   Failures from missing fixtures or unrelated imports were there before you: ignore them.\n\n# FINISH\n1. One shell command: git status --short && git diff. Remove any scratch file in /workspace; restore any changed test\n   file with git checkout -- path.\n2. Reply in plain text with NO tool call: one line saying what you changed and where. That reply hands over to your\n   teammate.\n\n# DECISION RULES\n- Ambiguous issue: take the most literal reading and act on it. Never ask questions.\n- Several candidate places: choose where the wrong behaviour is produced, not where it is observed.\n- A fix failed: make a different, smaller change. Never repeat the same edit.\n- Never conclude that nothing needs to change: every task needs a non-empty source patch.\n\n# THE ISSUE (verbatim; the task message may later be replaced by a summary, this copy stays)\n{problem_description}\n', 'skills/work/SKILL.md': '---\nname: work\ndescription: The fixer\'s shell. run_skill_script with skill_name work, file_path scripts/run.py and positional_args,\n  a list holding one string, the whole shell command. Runs in /workspace; the output ends with a clock line.\n---\n\nscripts/run.py runs one shell command in /workspace (output cut at 5000 characters) and ends with\n"[clock] N s of 360 used | ..." saying whether a source file is edited and what to do next. With no source edit at\n270 s it refuses commands until edit_file has changed a source file. 60 s after the repro prints FIXED it runs only\nfinishing commands (git status, git diff, git checkout --, rm).\n', 'skills/work/scripts/run.py': '"""sq1c2f6\'s shell (skill "work", scripts/run.py): sq1c2\'s clock shell plus two finish events, so runs end sooner\nwithout touching the first 270 s. Every output ends with a clock line (time used, source edited or not).\n\n- Before 270 s: as sq1c2 (warning from 180 s with no source edit, refusal from 270 s until a source file is edited).\n- Event A: a command prints a line starting with FIXED (the repro passes) while a source file is edited -> the clock\n  says to finish; FIXED_GRACE s later the finish window opens.\n- Event B: from FINISH_AT s with a source file edited, the finish window opens.\n- In the finish window only finishing commands run (git status / git diff / git checkout -- / rm); edit_file still\n  works, so a last correction is possible.\n\n    run_skill_script skill_name=work file_path=scripts/run.py positional_args=["git grep -n foo"]\n"""\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nSESSION = 360  # max_time_minutes 6 (sq1c2a6)\nWARN_AT = 180  # as sq1c2: no source edit by now -> warn\nREFUSE_AT = 270  # as sq1c2: no source edit by now -> refuse commands until one exists\nFINISH_AT = None  # sq1c2a6: event B off\nFIXED_GRACE = 60  # event A: finish window opens this long after the repro first printed FIXED\nOUT_MAX = 5000  # as the harness\'s run_command output limit\nEDIT_CMD = re.compile(r"sed -i|git apply|\\bpatch\\b|open\\([^)]*[\'\\"][wa][\'\\"]|write_text\\(|>\\s*(?!/tmp|/dev/null|&)\\S")\nFINISH_CMD = re.compile(r"^\\s*(git (status|diff|checkout --)|rm )[^;|&`$\\n]*(&&\\s*git (status|diff)[^;|&`$\\n]*)*$")\nFIXED_RE = re.compile(r"^\\s*FIXED\\b", re.M)\nTEST_RE = re.compile(r"(^|/)(tests?|testing)/|(^|/)test_[^/]*\\.py$|_test\\.py$|(^|/)conftest\\.py$|(^|/)pytest\\.ini$")\n\n\ndef workspace():\n    """The repository root: the skill wrapper chdirs into a temp dir, so find the directory it started in."""\n    import inspect\n    for frame in inspect.stack():\n        cwd = frame.frame.f_locals.get("_orig_cwd")\n        if isinstance(cwd, str) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cwd, ".git")):\n            return cwd\n    for cand in ("/workspace", os.getcwd()):\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cand, ".git")):\n            return cand\n    return os.getcwd()\n\n\ndef run_group(cmd, ws, timeout):\n    """bash -c CMD in its own process group; the whole group is killed when the command ends or times out, as the\n    harness\'s run_command does (adk_eval_core subprocess_sandbox.py), so no runaway child outlives the call\n    (2026-11-02: an orphaned process froze a Kaggle run: tool calls slowed to 27 s, then no model calls at all)."""\n    p = subprocess.Popen(["bash", "-c", cmd], cwd=ws, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, start_new_session=True)\n    timed_out = False\n    try:\n        out, err = p.communicate(timeout=timeout)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        timed_out = True\n    try:\n        os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):\n        pass\n    if timed_out:\n        try:\n            out, err = p.communicate(timeout=5)\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            out, err = "", ""\n    return p.returncode, out or "", err or "", timed_out\n\n\ndef sh(cmd, ws, timeout=30):\n    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=ws, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n    return r.returncode, r.stdout\n\n\ndef state_path(ws):\n    return os.path.join(ws, ".git", "agent", "clock.json")\n\n\ndef load_state(ws):\n    try:\n        return json.load(open(state_path(ws)))\n    except Exception:\n        return {}\n\n\ndef save_state(ws, state):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(state_path(ws)), exist_ok=True)\n    json.dump(state, open(state_path(ws), "w"))\n\n\ndef started(ws, state):\n    """Session start: the harness tags _swegemma_baseline when the sandbox starts; else the first run.py call."""\n    code, out = sh(["git", "log", "-1", "--format=%ct", "_swegemma_baseline"], ws)\n    if code == 0 and out.strip().isdigit():\n        return int(out.strip())\n    if "t0" not in state:\n        state["t0"] = time.time()\n        save_state(ws, state)\n    return state["t0"]\n\n\ndef edited(ws):\n    """Changed or new source files (not tests, not scratch files)."""\n    _, out = sh(["git", "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all"], ws)\n    files = [line[3:].split(" -> ")[-1].strip(\'"\') for line in out.splitlines() if len(line) > 3]\n    return [f for f in files if not TEST_RE.search(f) and not os.path.basename(f).startswith("repro")]\n\n\ndef command():\n    """The command from positional args (or args {"cmd": "..."}, argv --cmd X)."""\n    argv = [a for a in sys.argv[1:] if a != "--"]\n    if argv[:1] == ["--cmd"]:\n        argv = argv[1:]\n    elif argv[:1] and argv[0].startswith("--"):\n        argv = argv[1:]\n    return " ".join(argv).strip()\n\n\ndef finish_opens(used, state):\n    """Seconds into the session at which the finish window opens (given a source edit)."""\n    opens = float(\'inf\') if FINISH_AT is None else FINISH_AT\n    if "fixed_at" in state:\n        opens = min(opens, state["fixed_at"] + FIXED_GRACE)\n    return opens\n\n\ndef main():\n    ws = workspace()\n    state = load_state(ws)\n    used = int(time.time() - started(ws, state))\n    cmd = command()\n    files = edited(ws)\n    if not cmd:\n        body = "NO COMMAND: pass it as positional_args, a list holding one string: the whole shell command."\n    elif not files and used >= REFUSE_AT and not EDIT_CMD.search(cmd):\n        body = (f"REFUSED: {used} s of {SESSION} used and no source file is edited yet. An unedited tree scores zero; "\n                "a best guess can still be corrected. Your next call must be edit_file on the most likely place "\n                "(where the wrong behaviour is produced). Commands run again once a source file is edited.")\n    elif files and used >= finish_opens(used, state) and not FINISH_CMD.match(cmd):\n        body = (f"REFUSED: FINISH NOW ({used} s of {SESSION} used, source edited: {\', \'.join(files[:4])}). Only "\n                "git status, git diff, git checkout -- TESTFILE and rm SCRATCHFILE run now. Check the diff once, "\n                "then reply in plain text with no tool call: one line on what you changed and where.")\n    else:\n        code, out, err, timed_out = run_group(cmd, ws, max(5, min(150, SESSION - used - 10)))\n        body = (out + (("\\n[stderr]\\n" + err) if err.strip() else "")).rstrip()\n        body += "\\n[timed out: the command and everything it started were stopped]" if timed_out else f"\\n[exit {code}]"\n        if len(body) > OUT_MAX:\n            body = body[:OUT_MAX] + f"\\n[output cut at {OUT_MAX} characters: narrow the command]"\n        files = edited(ws)\n        if files and "fixed_at" not in state and FIXED_RE.search(body):\n            state["fixed_at"] = used\n            save_state(ws, state)\n    if files and used >= finish_opens(used, state):\n        state_txt = "source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4]) + " | FINISH NOW: git status && git diff, then the one-line reply"\n    elif files and "fixed_at" in state:\n        state_txt = ("source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4]) + f" | REPRO PASSES: run at most one related test file, "\n                     f"then FINISH; from {finish_opens(used, state)} s only finishing commands run")\n    elif files:\n        state_txt = "source edited: " + ", ".join(files[:4])\n    elif used >= WARN_AT:\n        state_txt = (f"NO SOURCE EDIT YET. Make your best edit now with edit_file; at {REFUSE_AT} s commands are "\n                     "refused until a source file is edited")\n    else:\n        state_txt = "no source edit yet"\n    print(body + f"\\n[clock] {used} s of {SESSION} used | {state_txt}")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n'}}
